  "details": "Concept for this is for anyone using VRC to produce content, like if they are singing they could be in an auditorium map and place cameras from different audience positions and on their camera controls be able to switch between them for the streamed output and add production value to the performance.\n\nThis could work for talk show formats too, where the camera could be switched to the person talking, if these cameras are shared then a camera person could be able to move the shared camera and others linked views of that camera move, and being shared there could be someone taking the role of producer viewing and switching the output between the cameras, maybe even from desktop view while people featured are in VR\n\nIf you were doing this regularly it might be finiky to place them each time so maps could have preset attach points for cameras or cameras that are just already in the map.\n\nThis would allow creating virtual TV studios or events, a lot of twitch streamers are making use of a camera person these days and it could work to bring that to VRC",
